  ('4e7de538-6ee8-5da5-931a-18b86bf726d3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The root chron means "time," and the suffix -logy can mean "an account of." What does "chronology" mean in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A scientific study of how metals react to heat","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A list of the designer's models ranked by their cost","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"A collection of drawings that show how a clock works","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"An account of events arranged in the order they happened","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An account of events arranged in the order they happened$q$, $q$A chronology is an account organized by time, which is why the passage says it "shows a steady shift" from large frames to a small device over decades. A ranking by cost ignores the time meaning of chron.$q$, 'draft', 'a20ce9b9-aa4e-5b16-b827-5dbdd987f7a5')
