   $q$The suffix -ize turns the noun "theory" into a verb. What does "theorized" mean in the sentence about the scholars?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Observed the stars through a telescope","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Rejected an idea after careful study","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Proved an idea through repeated experiments","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-certainty"},{"text":"Proposed an idea as a possible explanation","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Proposed an idea as a possible explanation$q$, $q$To theorize is to form a theory, a proposed explanation, and the scholars only believed the answer "lay in the stars." Nothing in the passage says they proved it, so the choice "Proved an idea through repeated experiments" claims too much certainty.$q$, 'draft', 'a20ce9b9-aa4e-5b16-b827-5dbdd987f7a5')
