   $q$The Latin prefix ambi- means "both," and dexter means "right hand" or "skillful." What does "ambidextrous" mean in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Able to play two different sports at a high level","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Able to move quickly in either direction on the field","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Able to use only the right hand with real skill","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"Able to use either hand with nearly equal skill","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Able to use either hand with nearly equal skill$q$, $q$Ambi plus dexter means "skillful on both sides," and the passage says these athletes can "throw, catch, or strike with either hand." Playing two sports uses "both" in the wrong sense, since the word is about hands.$q$, 'draft', 'dc3eaa1d-85e2-5b3d-979e-c317babdffc8')
