   $q$The suffix -ence turns the adjective "competent" into a noun. What does "competence" mean in the final paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A habit of avoiding the weaker hand","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A rule that limits how a hand is used","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A desire to win against other players","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"An adequate level of ability or skill","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An adequate level of ability or skill$q$, $q$Competent means capable, so competence is the state of being capable, here skill with the weaker hand. The desire to win describes competitiveness, a word that looks similar but has a different meaning.$q$, 'draft', 'dc3eaa1d-85e2-5b3d-979e-c317babdffc8')
