  ('f2525b70-b00b-5597-bcef-48d8d368b412', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The Greek root anthropo means "human," and -logy means "study of." What does the label "Anthropology" tell Hana about the room?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It holds materials for studying rocks and soil.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"It holds materials for studying the town's banking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"It holds materials for studying human life and culture.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It holds materials for studying animals of the valley.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It holds materials for studying human life and culture.$q$, $q$Anthropology is the study of humans, and Dr. Adeyemi explains the room holds "Anything human." The building was once a bank, but that detail does not explain the label.$q$, 'draft', '2b8d33eb-bae9-53db-a112-7bad5ec265b4')
