  ('47962d6a-249e-5c3c-9fd2-a21808f6f33e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The root phil means "love," anthropo means "human," and -ist means "a person who." What does calling Mr. Castellanos a "philanthropist" suggest about him?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He prefers to keep his wealth to himself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"He studies the history of the valley's families.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"He collects old toys and letters as a hobby.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"He generously gives money to help other people.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He generously gives money to help other people.$q$, $q$A philanthropist acts out of love for humanity, usually by donating, and Mr. Castellanos gave money to the museum, library, and clinic for thirty years. Studying human history describes an anthropologist, not a philanthropist.$q$, 'draft', '2b8d33eb-bae9-53db-a112-7bad5ec265b4')
