values
  ('497f823a-5d02-56e3-a642-96870ea56cfb', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The Greek prefix mis- can mean "hatred of," and anthropo means "human." What did Clara first believe about her neighbor when she called him a "misanthrope"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That he was too ill to attend the picnics","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"That he was generous to everyone in town","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"That he had made a serious mistake","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-prefix-meaning"},{"text":"That he disliked and avoided other people","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That he disliked and avoided other people$q$, $q$A misanthrope dislikes humankind, which matches a man who "refused to attend town picnics and scowled" at children. The English prefix mis- in words like misjudge means "wrongly," but here the Greek mis- means hatred, so "made a mistake" confuses the two.$q$, 'draft', '2b8d33eb-bae9-53db-a112-7bad5ec265b4')
