   $q$The root path means "disease," and gen means "produce" or "cause." What is a "pathogen"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A sign that a plant needs more water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A living thing that causes disease","is_correct":true},{"text":"A chemical that cures a sick plant","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A tree that resists all infections","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A living thing that causes disease$q$, $q$A pathogen produces disease, and the passage names examples such as "a fungus, bacterium, or virus." A cure is the opposite of something that causes illness.$q$, 'draft', '995df5ae-8188-5b3e-9d61-2a6ea1f2e03c')
