  ('520097fb-8beb-52d7-9d38-1ae5e96233b7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The prefix dis- can mean "remove" or "reverse," and credit comes from the root cred, "believe." What was the reader trying to do by attempting to "discredit" the find?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Remove the article from the newspaper's website","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Make people doubt that the discovery was genuine","is_correct":true},{"text":"Prove scientifically that the rock was a meteorite","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Give Elias credit for finding the meteorite","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Make people doubt that the discovery was genuine$q$, $q$To discredit is to remove belief in something, and the reader suggested the rock "had been bought online," casting doubt on the story. Taking "remove" too literally as deleting the article misses that the prefix reverses belief, not the article itself.$q$, 'draft', '059c876a-b458-587c-a6b4-bdc4eeabf8a8')
