  ('8141e683-006e-5c7d-acdf-66a66e20ae91', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The Latin prefix omni- means "all." What does it mean that seismic activity is "nearly omnipresent"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is strong enough for everyone to feel it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It is happening only in a few dangerous places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It is happening almost everywhere, almost all the time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is recorded by only one instrument at a time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is happening almost everywhere, almost all the time.$q$, $q$Omnipresent means present in all places, matching "thousands of small tremors around the world every day." The passage says no one may feel them, so the choice "It is strong enough for everyone to feel it" contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', 'b645b244-bb93-53d6-81a6-6f139575506a')
