   $q$The prefix omni- means "all." What can the "omnidirectional" sensors do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Point people in the direction of safety","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Send warnings to every city in the world","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Measure motion from one direction at a time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Detect motion coming from any direction","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Detect motion coming from any direction$q$, $q$Omni plus directional means "in all directions," and the passage says the sensors detect motion "from the north, the south, or directly below." Sending warnings everywhere stretches "all" to the wrong idea.$q$, 'draft', 'b645b244-bb93-53d6-81a6-6f139575506a')
