  ('ca72ee9c-be2e-55d7-a9c3-c4a93fdcc7b7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The suffix -ize turns the noun "standard" into a verb meaning "to make." What did seismologists do when they had to "standardize" their methods?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Replace all their instruments every few years","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Make their methods consistent so results could be compared","is_correct":true},{"text":"Raise their methods to a higher level of difficulty","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"Keep their methods secret from other countries","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Make their methods consistent so results could be compared$q$, $q$To standardize is to make things follow one standard, which is why stations "use similar instruments and shared formulas." Raising the difficulty confuses a standard as a common rule with a standard as a high bar.$q$, 'draft', 'b645b244-bb93-53d6-81a6-6f139575506a')
