   $q$The Latin root culp means "blame" or "fault," and the suffix -able means "able to be" or "deserving." What does Ms. Petrova mean when she says "No one here is culpable"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"No player is able to fix the broken clock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"No player is allowed to keep playing the game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"No player understands the tournament's rules.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"No player deserves to be blamed for the problem.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$No player deserves to be blamed for the problem.$q$, $q$Culpable means deserving blame, and she adds that it is "not anyone's doing," which answers Rafael's fear that "he would be blamed." The suffix -able might suggest ability to fix, but the root culp points to fault, not repair.$q$, 'draft', '5a92fa28-9abe-56ef-82f3-14efcea084e7')
