   $q$The noun "theory" becomes the adjective "theoretical" when the suffix -ical is added. What does Kofi mean when he says his skill was "mostly theoretical" before the tournament?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It was fully tested through many years of paid work as an interpreter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It existed as an idea he believed in, but he had not yet used it in a real situation.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It was something he doubted and planned to give up studying after the event.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It was based on scientific experiments he had carried out with his family.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-term"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It existed as an idea he believed in, but he had not yet used it in a real situation.$q$, $q$Theoretical describes something that exists in idea rather than practice, and Kofi contrasts "I knew I could translate" with "Today I actually did it." Years of paid work would make his skill practical, the opposite of theoretical.$q$, 'draft', '5a92fa28-9abe-56ef-82f3-14efcea084e7')
